1
00:04:05,714 --> 00:04:11,714
Singing in her first movie musical!

2
00:08:11,428 --> 00:08:17,428
Barbie as The Princess & the Pauper is a animation,
family, comedy film directed by William Lau.

3
00:12:17,142 --> 00:12:23,142
In her first animated musical featuring seven original songs, Barbie comes to life in this modern
re-telling of a classic tale of mistaken identity and the power of friendship.

4
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:28,857
Based on the story by Mark Twain.

5
00:20:28,571 --> 00:20:34,571
Princess Anneliese / Erika (voice), played by Kelly Sheridan.

6
00:24:34,285 --> 00:24:40,285
Princess Anneliese (singing voice), played by Melissa Lyons.

7
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Erika (singing voice), played by Julie Stevens.

8
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:51,714
King Dominick (voice), played by Mark Hildreth.

9
00:36:51,428 --> 00:36:57,428
King Dominick (singing voice), played by Mark Luna.

10
00:40:57,142 --> 00:41:03,142
Julian (voice), played by Alessandro Juliani.

11
00:45:02,857 --> 00:45:08,857
Barbie as the Princess and the Pauper is a 2004 animated musical fantasy film.

12
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:14,571
It was released to video on September 28, 2004, and made its
television premiere on Nickelodeon on November 14, 2004.

13
00:53:14,285 --> 00:53:20,285
This film is the first musical in the Barbie series.

14
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
It was directed by William Lau and stars the voice of Kelly Sheridan as
the Barbie protagonists, Princess Anneliese and Erika.

15
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
The plot is loosely inspired by the 1881 Mark Twain novel The Prince and the Pauper, and it is the first Barbie film that
completely excludes fantastic elements (fairies, magic, mermaids), which were a usual part of Barbie franchise.

16
01:05:31,428 --> 01:05:37,428
It is generally regarded as one of the best films in the
franchise and has secured a strong cult following.

17
01:09:37,142 --> 01:09:43,142
Songs for the film were composed by Amy Powers, Megan Cavallari and
Rob Hudnut, who also executive-produced the film.

18
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
The film was nominated for six DVD Exclusive Awards.

19
01:17:48,571 --> 01:17:54,571
The film explores themes of princess, musical, based on
toy, female protagonist, identity swap.

20
01:21:54,285 --> 01:22:00,285
The tone is lighthearted.
